WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.301 --> 00:00:03.969
Bladesmiths,
welcome to the Forge.

00:00:04.069 --> 00:00:06.139
Every bladesmith
has a favorite knife.

00:00:08.908 --> 00:00:10.476
[all chuckling]

00:00:10.543 --> 00:00:12.812
[host] Gentlemen,
I have here a dagger,

00:00:12.978 --> 00:00:17.316
a kukri, a karambit,
a coffin-handle Bowie

00:00:17.450 --> 00:00:18.718
and a jambiya.

00:00:18.818 --> 00:00:20.453
You will need to choose
a blade style

00:00:20.620 --> 00:00:23.088
and combine it
with a different knife's handle

00:00:23.155 --> 00:00:25.858
in order to create
your own mash-up blade.

00:00:26.459 --> 00:00:28.961
Good luck.
Your three hours starts now.

00:00:29.095 --> 00:00:30.897
<i> Combining two different blades
 into one,</i>

00:00:31.030 --> 00:00:32.131
you have
to think about it.

00:00:32.465 --> 00:00:34.934
<i> 'Cause some of them</i> 
<i> may look cool on paper,</i> 

00:00:35.034 --> 00:00:36.469
but it's not gonna blend well

00:00:36.569 --> 00:00:38.871
unless you really look
into the details.

00:00:38.971 --> 00:00:40.372 line:0%
<i> I'm looking at these knives</i> 

00:00:40.439 --> 00:00:43.176 line:0%
and in the back of my mind
is Jay Neilson

00:00:43.676 --> 00:00:47.613 line:0%
swinging as hard as he can
on that deer antler.

00:00:48.280 --> 00:00:50.883
The blades have to be good
for an antler chop.

00:00:50.983 --> 00:00:53.720
It has to be good
for a fish slice.

00:00:53.820 --> 00:00:55.588
That's a lot
of different iterations.

00:00:56.089 --> 00:00:57.857
<i> I decide I'm gonna go</i> 
<i> with the kukri blade</i> 

00:00:58.024 --> 00:01:00.659 line:0%
<i> because I think it's the best</i> 
<i> design for the challenge.</i> 

00:01:00.759 --> 00:01:03.595 line:0%
<i> And I think it will marry up</i> 
<i> with that coffin handle.</i> 

00:01:03.696 --> 00:01:04.764
That's a winner.

00:01:04.931 --> 00:01:07.867
We've got a coffin-handle kukri
over here out of Vince as well.

00:01:08.033 --> 00:01:10.336
<i> I settle on</i> 
<i> the Bowie-knife blade.</i> 

00:01:10.470 --> 00:01:12.771
It's just
a tried and true blade

00:01:12.971 --> 00:01:14.173
and that karambit-style handle.

00:01:14.340 --> 00:01:16.175 line:0%
It's got a good feel to it.

00:01:16.242 --> 00:01:18.110 line:0%
When it's in the hand,
it's got a nice curve to it.

00:01:18.211 --> 00:01:21.146
<i> And I'm thinking</i> 
<i> that's gonna work for me.</i> 

00:01:21.246 --> 00:01:23.382
[Vince]<i> I wanna save time.</i> 

00:01:23.449 --> 00:01:25.418
<i> So I decided</i> 
<i> to draw the billet</i> 

00:01:25.451 --> 00:01:28.621
<i> and forge the knife</i> 
<i> simultaneously.</i> 

00:01:29.322 --> 00:01:31.290
Big Blue is a beast.

00:01:31.624 --> 00:01:33.726
<i> I need one of those</i> 
<i> in my shop.</i> 

00:01:34.293 --> 00:01:36.428
Now that they're
into the shaping phase,

00:01:36.562 --> 00:01:38.731
Big Blue can quickly
topple your metal.

00:01:38.831 --> 00:01:40.233
It can pop it flat.

00:01:40.967 --> 00:01:42.301
Ooh.

00:01:42.401 --> 00:01:43.569
Big Blue's got a lot of control

00:01:43.703 --> 00:01:46.539
and he gets away from me
and he crushes my tip.

00:01:46.673 --> 00:01:48.208
<i> At this point, I realize</i> 

00:01:48.241 --> 00:01:51.878
<i> the power tools allow me</i> 
<i> to move metal real quick,</i> 

00:01:51.978 --> 00:01:54.380
<i> but I'm getting</i> 
<i> to the detail work</i> 

00:01:54.446 --> 00:01:55.982
and at this point
they're dangerous.

00:01:56.482 --> 00:01:58.951
<i> I need to start</i> 
<i> doing this by hand.</i> 

00:01:59.018 --> 00:02:02.522
Ihope that crushed tip
is not an issue.

00:02:04.591 --> 00:02:06.693
Heat, beat, repeat!

00:02:06.793 --> 00:02:08.694
I'm done
pressing that steel down

00:02:08.794 --> 00:02:10.897
<i> to a workable size.</i> 

00:02:10.997 --> 00:02:13.966
So as I'm shaping this knife,
I'm working on the blade first.

00:02:14.099 --> 00:02:15.367 line:0%
But with a Bowie,

00:02:15.468 --> 00:02:17.203 line:0%
a lot of times you're gonna
put a guard on there

00:02:17.303 --> 00:02:18.605 line:0%
and maybe a hidden tang

00:02:18.738 --> 00:02:20.172 line:0%
or maybe a coffin tang.

00:02:20.305 --> 00:02:22.275
So I'm keeping
in the back of my head that,

00:02:22.375 --> 00:02:24.209
"Hey, this handle's
gonna be different

00:02:24.309 --> 00:02:26.212
than what a Bowie calls for."

00:02:26.312 --> 00:02:29.081
[host] Casey's Bowie's starting
to also take shape.

00:02:29.248 --> 00:02:30.316
[host 2]<i> I'm really liking</i> 
<i> the way</i> 

00:02:30.483 --> 00:02:32.117
<i> the Bowie-style blade</i> 
<i> is coming out,</i> 

00:02:32.251 --> 00:02:33.887
<i> but I'm worried</i> 
<i> about that karambit handle,</i> 

00:02:33.987 --> 00:02:35.455
<i> especially
 for the antler chop.</i> <i> </i>

00:02:36.289 --> 00:02:39.024
So I'm trying to put
the bend on this with my hammer

00:02:39.158 --> 00:02:40.593
and it's not working
really well.

00:02:41.093 --> 00:02:43.596
A kukri without the bend
is not a kukri.

00:02:43.663 --> 00:02:46.232
That's the defining factor
of a kukri.

00:02:46.332 --> 00:02:50.202
So, I need to figure out
how to put the bend in now.

00:02:50.670 --> 00:02:52.839
[Wil] We've got Shawn
on the horn of the anvil,

00:02:52.939 --> 00:02:54.773
really trying to knock
that belly,

00:02:54.873 --> 00:02:56.075
that inside curve

00:02:56.408 --> 00:02:58.310
into
the coffin-handled kukri.

00:02:58.343 --> 00:02:59.913
That's the way I shape kukris.

00:03:00.346 --> 00:03:03.415
[Shawn]<i> I've seen where</i> 
<i> people bang it over the horn</i> 

00:03:03.549 --> 00:03:06.786
<i> and gravity will naturally</i> 
<i> put that bend in,</i> <i> </i>

00:03:07.386 --> 00:03:09.856
and it bent down
right like I thought.

00:03:11.657 --> 00:03:13.860
<i> I'm done putting the bend</i> 
<i> in the kukri</i> 

00:03:13.960 --> 00:03:17.296
and I'm on to
profiling my handle

00:03:17.397 --> 00:03:19.465
to make sure that it looks
like a coffin handle.

00:03:19.532 --> 00:03:23.403
Right now Vince's tang section
is really fat.

00:03:24.002 --> 00:03:25.404
I chose to leave it thick

00:03:25.538 --> 00:03:29.208
because it's always easier
to remove material

00:03:29.308 --> 00:03:30.610
than it is to add on.

00:03:30.710 --> 00:03:32.544
It's time to go quench.

00:03:33.245 --> 00:03:34.480
[Jay] Vincejust quenched
his blade.

00:03:34.614 --> 00:03:35.981
Looked like
a good temperature.

00:03:36.015 --> 00:03:38.418
The handle
wasn't heated up at all.

00:03:39.384 --> 00:03:41.687
<i> I have no cracks, no warp</i> 

00:03:41.854 --> 00:03:43.322
<i> and I have a hard blade.</i> 

00:03:43.456 --> 00:03:45.124
I know I'm in great shape.

00:03:45.257 --> 00:03:48.060
-We did the same thing, bro.
-Yeah, buddy.

00:03:48.127 --> 00:03:49.562
Looks good, man.

00:03:50.863 --> 00:03:52.165
<i> My profile's done,</i> 

00:03:52.198 --> 00:03:54.199
<i> and I know</i> 
<i> what a good blade feels like.</i> 

00:03:54.299 --> 00:03:56.735
So in my hand
I'm swinging it around

00:03:56.869 --> 00:03:59.438
<i> to make sure it's not sliding</i> 
<i> around the hand,</i> 

00:03:59.471 --> 00:04:01.274
<i> not wanting</i> 
<i> to jump out of my grip.</i> 

00:04:01.674 --> 00:04:03.776
It's that time
for the heat treat.

00:04:05.444 --> 00:04:08.014
It's smart that Casey
didn't harden the whole blade

00:04:08.181 --> 00:04:10.249
because in one of those rings,
you forge it in,

00:04:10.383 --> 00:04:12.651
-always a lot of clean up.
-Yeah.

00:04:12.751 --> 00:04:15.521
<i> I'm hoping that nothing went</i> 
<i> catastrophically wrong.</i> 

00:04:15.655 --> 00:04:17.656
I don't wanna pull out
a banana.

00:04:18.524 --> 00:04:20.893
I bring it out and it's just
perfectly straight.

00:04:20.993 --> 00:04:22.961
All right. She sounds hard.

00:04:23.095 --> 00:04:25.197
<i> It's time to quench, so,</i> 

00:04:25.297 --> 00:04:26.866
<i> never having quenched W1,</i> 

00:04:26.999 --> 00:04:30.202
I'm very concerned about
the temperature of the blade.

00:04:30.803 --> 00:04:33.673
I just don't know.
Is that too [bleep] hot?

00:04:34.373 --> 00:04:35.541
-[sizzles]
-Oh!

00:04:35.975 --> 00:04:37.176
It's hotter than snot.

00:04:37.242 --> 00:04:39.211
That is no bueno.

00:04:39.879 --> 00:04:42.782
I have a soft spot in
the recurve of my blade.

00:04:43.416 --> 00:04:46.151
I bite the bullet
and do it again.

00:04:46.285 --> 00:04:48.354
Hopefully
it's going to harden.

00:04:49.321 --> 00:04:52.057
[Wil] Three, two, one!

00:04:52.191 --> 00:04:53.959
Bladesmiths,
shut down your machines!

00:04:54.060 --> 00:04:55.327
Drop your tools!

00:04:55.428 --> 00:04:58.197
This first round of mash-up
competition is over!

00:04:58.264 --> 00:04:59.299
Whoo!

00:05:01.066 --> 00:05:02.167
Bladesmiths, I know you had fun

00:05:02.334 --> 00:05:03.703
making these
mix-and-match weapons.

00:05:03.803 --> 00:05:05.371
But I know
this is your favorite part,

00:05:05.404 --> 00:05:07.073
the strength test.

00:05:08.040 --> 00:05:10.309
We're not only gonna test
the overall construction,

00:05:10.409 --> 00:05:12.612
but how well you designed
your mash-up weapons

00:05:12.679 --> 00:05:13.579
for these tests.

00:05:13.613 --> 00:05:14.714
What I'm gonna do is take

00:05:14.881 --> 00:05:17.083
each of your
mix-and-match weapons here

00:05:17.183 --> 00:05:20.586
and smash them repeatedly and
violently into these antlers.

00:05:20.753 --> 00:05:22.054
Now, keep in mind,

00:05:22.154 --> 00:05:24.356
I'm not concerned about what
your blades do to the antler.

00:05:24.423 --> 00:05:26.992
I wanna see what the antlers
do to your blades.

00:05:27.092 --> 00:05:28.160
Shawn, you're up first.

00:05:28.227 --> 00:05:29.261
[chuckles] Let's do it.

00:05:29.361 --> 00:05:31.731
[tense music playing]

00:05:32.264 --> 00:05:34.600
[grunting]

00:05:39.371 --> 00:05:40.439
-[men gasping]
-Watch out!

00:05:40.606 --> 00:05:42.742
[metal clanks on the floor]

00:05:45.110 --> 00:05:47.279
[tense music playing]

00:05:47.380 --> 00:05:49.015
[sighs] Damn.

00:05:50.183 --> 00:05:51.283
The warp's gone.

00:05:51.450 --> 00:05:53.019
The warp is gone.

00:05:55.120 --> 00:05:57.456
Your edge itself held up well.

00:05:57.556 --> 00:05:59.492
Just a small bit
of shine to it.

00:05:59.625 --> 00:06:01.093
And it bit in nicely,

00:06:01.560 --> 00:06:04.496
but you've got a pretty large
grain structure here.

00:06:05.030 --> 00:06:08.300
It was a little too high
a temperature when you quenched

00:06:08.400 --> 00:06:09.935
and if you look
at the bottom here,

00:06:10.002 --> 00:06:13.405
there's like a little bit
of a brownish discoloration.

00:06:13.538 --> 00:06:15.241
Means there was
a stress fracture in there.

00:06:15.341 --> 00:06:17.576
It could have been
too small to see it,

00:06:17.676 --> 00:06:20.780
but, obviously, it was there.

00:06:20.813 --> 00:06:21.714
Right.

00:06:24.517 --> 00:06:26.084
[Wil] Well, Shawn,
unfortunately,

00:06:26.218 --> 00:06:28.688
Jay has a way with blades.

00:06:28.755 --> 00:06:29.955
[chuckles] Yeah.

00:06:30.055 --> 00:06:33.125
Your blade has failed after
five strikes on the antler.

00:06:33.325 --> 00:06:34.693
It doesn't mean
that you're out,

00:06:34.794 --> 00:06:38.330
because each of you
have to survive five strikes

00:06:38.363 --> 00:06:40.699
in order to move forward
in this competition.

00:06:40.833 --> 00:06:41.801
Alright, Jay.

00:06:43.969 --> 00:06:46.171
Casey, after seeing
what happened to Shawn's blade,

00:06:46.305 --> 00:06:48.173
-how're you feeling?
-Give it hell.

00:06:48.307 --> 00:06:50.342
-[tense music playing]
-[grunting]

00:06:50.409 --> 00:06:54.414
[grunting continues]

00:06:55.114 --> 00:06:55.948
[grunts]

00:07:02.521 --> 00:07:03.623
[Wil] Casey, looks like

00:07:03.723 --> 00:07:06.358
your karambit-Bowie mash-up
survived.

00:07:06.425 --> 00:07:07.793
Great construction.

00:07:08.294 --> 00:07:10.463
Shawn, your fate
lies in the hands

00:07:10.630 --> 00:07:13.065
of how strong
Vince's blade is.

00:07:13.165 --> 00:07:14.066
Jay?

00:07:14.766 --> 00:07:17.369
[Vince]<i> All I need is</i> 
<i> for my blade to survive</i> 

00:07:17.469 --> 00:07:19.471
<i> five hits on that antler.</i> 

00:07:19.504 --> 00:07:22.140
My heart has never been
beating as hard

00:07:22.174 --> 00:07:23.709
as it is right now.

00:07:25.311 --> 00:07:27.113
-[tense music playing]
-[thumps]

00:07:28.013 --> 00:07:30.716
[grunting]

00:07:36.154 --> 00:07:38.458
[exhales sharply]

00:07:43.496 --> 00:07:46.232
Well, Vince, five successful
strikes on the antler

00:07:46.299 --> 00:07:47.866
pushes you forward
in this competition

00:07:48.033 --> 00:07:49.268
and unfortunately,

00:07:49.401 --> 00:07:51.337
pushes you
out of the competition, Shawn.

00:07:51.437 --> 00:07:53.072
Please exit the Forge.

00:07:54.239 --> 00:07:58.244
My goal coming here, A: don't
blow the place up... check.

00:07:58.277 --> 00:08:00.979
<i> And B: don't be the first guy</i> 
<i> that gets sent home.</i> 

00:08:01.547 --> 00:08:03.682
So, I did
what I came here to do.

00:08:03.815 --> 00:08:06.418
Anything else was gonna be
icing on the cake for me.

00:08:06.785 --> 00:08:09.621
<i> You have to do something</i> 
<i> you love and I still love it.</i> 

00:08:10.389 --> 00:08:11.858
I'm gonna go home
and make more blades

00:08:11.958 --> 00:08:12.959
soon as I get there.

